00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:44,420
and take them there immediately, is totally different.

292
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:45,900
But yeah, I agree,

293
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:50,900
Let the scouts buy into it and go with that direction.

294
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:53,780
Yeah, I think the last thing I would want to see

295
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:57,100
if I was running a community disaster training course

296
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,540
would be somebody showing up with 15 or 20 boys

297
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:02,920
who had absolutely no interest in it at all

298
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,480
because somebody just thought it was a good idea.

299
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:10,319
Right, that's what you have: spontaneous volunteers

300
00:15:10,319 --> 00:15:13,560
who are people who just show up and you know,

301
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:14,959
it's kind of like Little Rascals-

302
00:15:14,959 --> 00:15:16,599
hey, kids, let's make a movie.

303
00:15:16,599 --> 00:15:20,040
And then you've got typed resources,

304
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:21,760
and a typed resources says somebody

305
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:25,439
who can operate this radio, you know, with these forms

306
00:15:25,439 --> 00:15:26,280
and that kind of stuff.

307
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:29,079
And so if you have a typed resource,

308
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:32,940
then you can just say you go do this

309
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:36,180
and the problem is solved. but you'll never have enough.

310
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:39,140
You know, we've reflected that we're kind of ahead

311
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:42,900
of the game just because we're used to going camping.

312
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,820
You know, everybody has this kind of mindfulness

313
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,060
about watching out for each other

314
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:51,900
and everybody has at least a basic level

315
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,380
of first aid training.

316
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,460
The scouts have proven again and again

317
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,940
over the past century that they're very valuable

318
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,000
in emergencies.

319
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Most of these agencies, most of these response agencies,

320
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,020
want people to have a level of training,

321
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:09,400
And it's not necessarily a really sophisticated level

322
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:11,720
of training. it's just a little. you know

323
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:15,000
they want people not to create greater emergencies

324
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,160
by quote unquote helping out,

325
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:21,000
And so you'll need groups that are competent

326
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,160
but maybe not specific and you'll have holes to fill.

327
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:28,219
And I think that's really where the scouts are gonna fit in.

328
00:16:28,219 --> 00:16:30,819
And you know we have the ePREP Merit Badge

329
00:16:30,819 --> 00:16:34,300
which says: take place in a practice or a real emergency.

330
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,800
We can't schedule the real emergencies,

331
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:40,140
but those are, and maybe it's time for ePREP

332
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:43,140
to be updated with InstaCommand System.

333
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,140
I think that I'm really looking forward

334
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:46,500
to the search and rescue merit badge.

335
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,180
Yeah, that was just recently announced.

336
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,420
within the past couple of weeks,

337
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:54,300
new merit badge, SAR, search and rescue.

338
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:56,160
Have you looked at that any closer

339
00:16:56,160 --> 00:16:58,160
than the announcement at all? Walter,

340
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,860
I have not seen any requirements.

341
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:03,400
I've seen that the right people are involved

342
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:08,400
in doing the merit badge and kind of defining it.

343
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:12,100
And actually the new radio merit badge

