00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:15,080
was updated a little fairly recently

345
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:18,160
And there's been a big uptick in radio merit badge

346
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,920
and involvement with the radio amateurs

347
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:24,920
and just communication. that's another thing to get trained in.

348
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,760
And are you a counselor for radio?

349
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,200
I have. I've taught the course a couple of times

350
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:35,880
And the guys like it. one of the things we do

351
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:39,400
is something like a scavenger hunt,

352
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,040
search and rescue kind of thing

353
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:43,720
where you've got somebody running net control

354
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:46,740
and a couple of teams out getting directions

355
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,600
And the updates to the merit badge

356
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:52,159
change things so that how did they change?

357
00:17:52,159 --> 00:17:54,159
So there's a regular kind of updating,

358
00:17:54,159 --> 00:17:58,480
but there's been a new memorandum of understanding

359
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:03,080
between the Scouts and AWRL about working on it.

360
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,919
There's several portable or not portable,

361
00:18:05,919 --> 00:18:09,360
but loaner radio stations now available

362
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:12,719
from National that were donated by ICOM

363
00:18:12,719 --> 00:18:14,399
So people can sign up for that

364
00:18:14,399 --> 00:18:18,240
and get a multiple radio set up for a special event

365
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,520
for summer camp.

366
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,880
This sort of goes back to the emergency prep stuff.

367
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:25,000
for the first day there was a cub pack.

368
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,320
We use them as our patients

369
00:18:28,320 --> 00:18:30,180
and they put them out on the playground

370
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:32,160
like this kid fell out of the swing

371
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:34,680
and there's a little chicken bone with some blood

372
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,200
sticking out of the shirt

373
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,840
And we'd have the patrols go out

374
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:42,400
and assess what had just happened to this kid

375
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:45,760
and perform the appropriate first day.

376
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:48,840
Yeah, scenarios are tremendous for teaching first aid

377
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:51,200
and moulage the fake wounds.

378
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,760
If you get actually get the guys into that,

379
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:55,720
that can be really, really fun.

380
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:59,000
I'm not sure that having the guys come up

